Revision history for Ham-CW

0.001  2026-10-24
    - Add an optional PDL backend for faster audio generation, PCM conversion
      and tone detection. Select it with backend => 'pdl'; existing callers
      continue to use the Perl implementation by default.
    - Allow automatic backend selection and a per-call reception override.
      Keep the existing sample arrays, streaming limits and error codes.
    - Add numerical equivalence tests, a reproducible benchmark and PDL test
      jobs for Linux, macOS and Windows. The completed platform checks and
      PCM measurements are recorded in docs/verification.md.
    - Expand FAST CI to the minimum Perl/PDL combination and macOS Intel.
      Use Strawberry Perl for native Windows builds, save benchmark evidence,
      and compare all PCM depths as well as streaming reception.
    - Make missing-PDL tests portable to Perl 5.20.
    - Initial development release.
    - International Morse text, explicit prosigns and Farnsworth timing.
    - Cumulative event conversion and deterministic PCM synthesis.
    - Bounded PCM WAV reading and writing at 8, 16 and 24 bits.
    - Experimental Goertzel reception and incremental processing.

    - Fix sparse audio detection, retain partially decoded text, expose reception
    limits and clarify spectral diagnostics. Validate inferred Farnsworth timing,
    low-rate defaults and PCM bit depth. Add operational prosign aliases and
    regression coverage; tolerate trailing WAV bytes with a warning.
